      <header class="e-head">
        <div><span class="e-num">03</span><span class="e-of">/ 25</span></div>
        <div class="e-id"><p class="e-tag">Item 03 · Trade: Finance · A.A.B.B.A. · 5 lines</p><h2 class="e-name">Bill the Economist</h2></div>
      </header>
      <div class="e-body">
        <div class="verse">
          <p class="lm"><span class="lm-i">There was a Bill, the economist,</span></p>
          <p class="lm"><span class="lm-i">A graph-poring, currency skeptic</span></p>
          <p class="lm"><span class="lm-i">Of markets and yield;</span></p>
          <p class="lm"><span class="lm-i">“Each bull run will kneel”</span></p>
          <p class="lm"><span class="lm-i">“The bear always wins,” he’d say, that economist.</span></p>
        </div>
        <aside class="e-side">
          <figure class="photo"><img src="https://picsum.photos/seed/bill-the-economist/240/300" alt="Portrait No. 03 — Bill the Economist" width="240" height="300" loading="lazy"><figcaption>Portrait No. 03</figcaption></figure>
          <p class="note"><span class="n-label">Note</span>Sage of the ledger; last seen at the 25-cent Economist stall, arguing with a chart.</p>
        </aside>
      </div>
      <span class="stamp e-stamp">Audited</span>
    </article>
    <div class="perf" aria-hidden="true"></div>

    <article class="entry reveal" id="item-04">
      <header class="e-head">
        <div><span class="e-num">04</span><span class="e-of">/ 25</span></div>
        <div class="e-id"><p class="e-tag">Item 04 · Location: Hamburg · A.A.B.B.A. · 5 lines</p><h2 class="e-name">Bill &amp; Jurgen</h2></div>
      </header>
      <div class="e-body">
        <div class="verse">
          <p class="lm"><span class="lm-i">There once was a Bill in the Hamburg</span></p>
          <p class="lm"><span class="lm-i">Whom no card trick could ever have stumped —</span></p>
          <p class="lm"><span class="lm-i">Until there came Jurgen,</span></p>
          <p class="lm"><span class="lm-i">A Hessian burgher,</span></p>
          <p class="lm"><span class="lm-i">Who dealt with a grin, and Bill’s stack was all trumped.</span></p>
        </div>
        <aside class="e-side">
          <figure class="photo"><img src="https://picsum.photos/seed/bill-and-jurgen/240/300" alt="Portrait No. 04 — Bill at the card table with Jurgen" width="240" height="300" loading="lazy"><figcaption>Portrait No. 04</figcaption></figure>
          <p class="note"><span class="n-label">Note</span>The pot was paid by check. The check bounced. Jurgen declined to comment.</p>
        </aside>
      </div>
      <span class="stamp e-stamp">Disputed</span>
    </article>
    <div class="perf" aria-hidden="true"></div>

    <article class="entry reveal" id="item-05">
      <header class="e-head">
        <div><span class="e-num">05</span><span class="e-of">/ 25</span></div>
        <div class="e-id"><p class="e-tag">Item 05 · Object: Bell · A.A.B.B.A. · 5 lines</p><h2 class="e-name">Bill the Bell</h2></div>
      </header>
      <div class="e-body">
        <div class="verse">
          <p class="lm"><span class="lm-i">There once was a Bill the big bell,</span></p>
          <p class="lm"><span class="lm-i">A bronze one who rang with a rattle and swell;</span></p>
          <p class="lm"><span class="lm-i">No clapper could reach him,</span></p>
          <p class="lm"><span class="lm-i">No hammer would teach him,</span></p>
          <p class="lm"><span class="lm-i">Yet at half past eleven, he’d ring by himself.</span></p>
        </div>
        <aside class="e-side">
          <figure class="photo"><img src="https://picsum.photos/seed/bill-the-bell/240/300" alt="Portrait No. 05 — Bill the Bell" width="240" height="300" loading="lazy"><figcaption>Portrait No. 05</figcaption></figure>
          <p class="note"><span class="n-label">Note</span>Rings of his own accord. The clock tower billed the repairman, who was also a Bill.</p>
        </aside>
      </div>
      <span class="stamp e-stamp">Paid</span>
    </article>
    <div class="perf" aria-hidden="true"></div>

    <article class="entry reveal" id="item-06">
      <header class="e-head">
        <div><span class="e-num">06</span><span class="e-of">/ 25</span></div>
        <div class="e-id"><p class="e-tag">Item 06 · Trade: Bellringing · A.A.B.B.A. · 5 lines</p><h2 class="e-name">Bill the Bellman</h2></div>
      </header>
      <div class="e-body">
        <div class="verse">
          <p class="lm"><span class="lm-i">There once was a Bill who’d ring every door,</span></p>
          <p class="lm"><span class="lm-i">A bellman who’d wake the whole street and its floor;</span></p>
          <p class="lm"><span class="lm-i">“Ring softer, dear Bill!”</span></p>
          <p class="lm"><span class="lm-i">The neighbors would call,</span></p>
          <p class="lm"><span class="lm-i">But the good man was deaf, and the jingle rang more.</span></p>
        </div>
        <aside class="e-side">
          <figure class="photo"><img src="https://picsum.photos/seed/bill-the-bellman/240/300" alt="Portrait No. 06 — Bill the Bellman" width="240" height="300" loading="lazy"><figcaption>Portrait No. 06</figcaption></figure>
          <p class="note"><span class="n-label">Note</span>Deaf since 1803. The neighbors have since learned to ring their own.</p>
        </aside>
      </div>
      <span class="stamp e-stamp">Cleared</span>
    </article>
    <div class="perf" aria-hidden="true"></div>

    <article class="entry reveal" id="item-07">
      <header class="e-head">
        <div><span class="e-num">07</span><span class="e-of">/ 25</span></div>
        <div class="e-id"><p class="e-tag">Item 07 · Specimen: Bovine · A.A.B.B.A. · 5 lines</p><h2 class="e-name">Bill the Bull</h2></div>
      </header>
      <div class="e-body">
        <div class="verse">
          <p class="lm"><span class="lm-i">There once was a Bill the bull,</span></p>
          <p class="lm"><span class="lm-i">Whose horn was a magnificent, terrible tool;</span></p>
          <p class="lm"><span class="lm-i">He’d charge at the farmer,</span></p>
          <p class="lm"><span class="lm-i">But never at barley —</span></p>
          <p class="lm"><span class="lm-i">For the cows would attest, with a low, that he had a soul.</span></p>
        </div>
        <aside class="e-side">
          <figure class="photo"><img src="https://picsum.photos/seed/bill-the-bull/240/300" alt="Portrait No. 07 — Bill the Bull" width="240" height="300" loading="lazy"><figcaption>Portrait No. 07</figcaption></figure>
          <p class="note"><span class="n-label">Note</span>The only Bill on this ledger who has ever been a full head of cattle.</p>
        </aside>
      </div>
      <span class="stamp e-stamp">Balanced</span>
    </article>
    <div class="perf" aria-hidden="true"></div>

    <article class="entry reveal" id="item-08">
      <header class="e-head">
        <div><span class="e-num">08</span><span class="e-of">/ 25</span></div>
        <div class="e-id"><p class="e-tag">Item 08 · Tool: Billhook · A.A.B.B.A. · 5 lines</p><h2 class="e-name">Bill the Billhook</h2></div>
      </header>
      <div class="e-body">
        <div class="verse">
          <p class="lm"><span class="lm-i">There once was a Bill with a billhook</span></p>
          <p class="lm"><span class="lm-i">And, being of a sentimental blood,</span></p>
          <p class="lm"><span class="lm-i">He named the dear iron,</span></p>
          <p class="lm"><span class="lm-i">He called it good morning,</span></p>
          <p class="lm"><span class="lm-i">“Good day, dear Bill,” said he — and the meadow shook.</span></p>
        </div>
        <aside class="e-side">
          <figure class="photo"><img src="https://picsum.photos/seed/bill-the-billhook/240/300" alt="Portrait No. 08 — Bill the Billhook" width="240" height="300" loading="lazy"><figcaption>Portrait No. 08</figcaption></figure>
          <p class="note"><span class="n-label">Note</span>The tool and its owner argue about who is really named Bill.</p>
        </aside>
      </div>
      <span class="stamp e-stamp">Paid</span>
    </article>
    <div class="perf" aria-hidden="true"></div>

    <article class="entry reveal" id="item-09">
      <header class="e-head">
        <div><span class="e-num">09</span><span class="e-of">/ 25</span></div>
        <div class="e-id"><p class="e-tag">Item 09 · Phenomenon: Wave · A.A.B.B.A. · 5 lines</p><h2 class="e-name">Bill the Billow</h2></div>
      </header>
      <div class="e-body">
        <div class="verse">
          <p class="lm"><span class="lm-i">There once was a Bill the billow,</span></p>
          <p class="lm"><span class="lm-i">A wave off a coast where the foam was a mellow yellow;</span></p>
          <p class="lm"><span class="lm-i">He’d rise, and he’d crash,</span></p>
          <p class="lm"><span class="lm-i">And he’d foam, and he’d splash,</span></p>
          <p class="lm"><span class="lm-i">And the fishermen called him “a dear, dear fellow.”</span></p>
        </div>
        <aside class="e-side">
          <figure class="photo"><img src="https://picsum.photos/seed/bill-the-billow/240/300" alt="Portrait No. 09 — Bill the Billow" width="240" height="300" loading="lazy"><figcaption>Portrait No. 09</figcaption></figure>
          <p class="note"><span class="n-label">Note</span>A wave; a billow; a break. The fishermen’s union has filed a bill of particulars.</p>
        </aside>
      </div>
      <span class="stamp e-stamp">Cleared</span>
    </article>
    <div class="perf" aria-hidden="true"></div>

    <article class="entry reveal" id="item-10">
      <header class="e-head">
        <div><span class="e-num">10</span><span class="e-of">/ 25</span></div>
        <div class="e-id"><p class="e-tag">Item 10 · Specimen: Duck · A.A.B.B.A. · 5 lines</p><h2 class="e-name">Bill the Duck</h2></div>
      </header>
      <div class="e-body">
        <div class="verse">
          <p class="lm"><span class="lm-i">There once was a duck named simply Bill,</span></p>
          <p class="lm"><span class="lm-i">Who’d sign all his deals with a beak of quill;</span></p>
          <p class="lm"><span class="lm-i">No ink, and no nib,</span></p>
          <p class="lm"><span class="lm-i">Just a “quack” and a dip</span></p>
          <p class="lm"><span class="lm-i">In the pond — and the bank would decline all his will.</span></p>
        </div>
        <aside class="e-side">
          <figure class="photo"><img src="https://picsum.photos/seed/bill-the-duck/240/300" alt="Portrait No. 10 — Bill the Duck" width="240" height="300" loading="lazy"><figcaption>Portrait No. 10</figcaption></figure>
          <p class="note"><span class="n-label">Note</span>The bank will not cash a quack’s signature. The duck disputes the fee.</p>
        </aside>
      </div>
      <span class="stamp e-stamp">Disputed</span>
    </article>
    <div class="perf" aria-hidden="true"></div>

    <article class="entry reveal" id="item-11">
      <header class="e-head">
        <div><span class="e-num">11</span><span class="e-of">/ 25</span></div>
        <div class="e-id"><p class="e-tag">Item 11 · Specimen: Lark · A.A.B.B.A. · 5 lines</p><h2 class="e-name">Bill the Billed Lark</h2></div>
      </header>
      <div class="e-body">
        <div class="verse">
          <p class="lm"><span class="lm-i">There once was a Bill the billed lark</span></p>
          <p class="lm"><span class="lm-i">Whose bill of fare was four thousand songs from the park;</span></p>
          <p class="lm"><span class="lm-i">He’d sing them all through,</span></p>
          <p class="lm"><span class="lm-i">Then sing them again, new —</span></p>
          <p class="lm"><span class="lm-i">And faint in the field, and the meadow was dark.</span></p>
        </div>
        <aside class="e-side">
          <figure class="photo"><img src="https://picsum.photos/seed/bill-the-lark/240/300" alt="Portrait No. 11 — Bill the Billed Lark" width="240" height="300" loading="lazy"><figcaption>Portrait No. 11</figcaption></figure>
          <p class="note"><span class="n-label">Note</span>A billed lark; a bill of four thousand songs; one (1) encore, unpaid.</p>
        </aside>
      </div>
      <span class="stamp e-stamp">Paid</span>
    </article>
    <div class="perf" aria-hidden="true"></div>

    <article class="entry reveal" id="item-12">
      <header class="e-head">
        <div><span class="e-num">12</span><span class="e-of">/ 25</span></div>
        <div class="e-id"><p class="e-tag">Item 12 · Currency: USD (Five) · A.A.B.B.A. · 5 lines</p><h2 class="e-name">Bill the Fifth</h2></div>
      </header>
      <div class="e-body">
        <div class="verse">
          <p class="lm"><span class="lm-i">There once was a Bill who was the fifth</span></p>
          <p class="lm"><span class="lm-i">(A dollar), who’d travel with a wonderful drift</span></p>
          <p class="lm"><span class="lm-i">Through every tip cup,</span></p>
          <p class="lm"><span class="lm-i">And every register,</span></p>
          <p class="lm"><span class="lm-i">And think he was worth much more than his self.</span></p>
        </div>
        <aside class="e-side">
          <figure class="photo"><img src="https://picsum.photos/seed/bill-the-fifth/240/300" alt="Portrait No. 12 — Bill the Fifth" width="240" height="300" loading="lazy"><figcaption>Portrait No. 12</figcaption></figure>
          <p class="note"><span class="n-label">Note</span>A five-dollar note; thinks of himself as more. The economist (item 03) disagrees.</p>
        </aside>
      </div>
      <span class="stamp e-stamp">Audited</span>
    </article>
    <div class="perf" aria-hidden="true"></div>

    <section class="memo reveal" aria-label="Office memorandum">
      <div class="memo-letter">
        <p class="memo-head">Office Memorandum</p>
        <p>Re: the word <b>“bill.”</b> The Office reminds its clients that the ledger above has been audited against every known sense of the word. The economist (item 03) has certified the meter at fourteen (14) anapests and one (1) apology. Jurgen (item 04) has reviewed the account and objects only to the rhyme “Jurgen / burgher,” which he calls “phonetically aggressive.” The Office notes that he has not once won the pot. — <i>The Auditor</i></p>
      </div>
      <div class="memo-table">
        <p class="memo-head">Definitions of “Bill”</p>
        <table>
          <thead><tr><th>Sense</th><th>Meaning</th><th>Seen at</th></tr></thead>
          <tbody>
            <tr><td>Person</td><td>A man named Bill</td><td>All 25 items</td></tr>
            <tr><td>Invoice</td><td>A demand for payment</td><td>13 · 17 · 20 · 21</td></tr>
            <tr><td>Beak</td><td>The bill of a bird (also “billed”)</td><td>10 · 11</td></tr>
